# Changelog

## [Unreleased]

### Breaking Changes

- A pre-0.2.0 database is not upgradeable: the migration tree is re-baselined to a single revision, and `alembic upgrade head` refuses a legacy-stamped database rather than migrating it — rebuild the database per `docs/Rebuilding the database.md`
- Retype `pipeline_runs.scope_id`, `graph_chunks.source_id`, `chunk_id`, and `mention_id` (with `mention_id_lo`/`mention_id_hi`) from string to `Uuid`
- `derivation_key` values are now opaque digests carrying a `derivation_key_format` version stamp, not human-readable composites
- Contextualization's stage functions take a resolved model configuration (provider and model) in place of a profile alias; every caller changes
- Default the picture-description model to `openai/gpt-5.6-luna`; the model name is part of the conversion output config hash, so conversions under the default re-key
- Raise dependency majors: `pydantic-ai` to 2.x, the OpenAI SDK to 3.x, `mcp` to 2.x, `starlette` to 1.x, `docling` to 2.124, and `torch` to 2.14 (cu130 index on Linux)
- Conversion job statuses are the six lowercase values `queued`, `running`, `succeeded`, `failed`, `cancelled`, and `timed_out`, in responses, the `status` filter, and the status-count keys; `NEW`, `QUEUED`, `RUNNING`, `UPLOAD_PENDING`, `SUCCEEDED`, `FAILED_RETRYABLE`, `FAILED_PERM`, and `CANCELLED` are gone, and a failed job's retry class is the new `retry_class` field
- Conversion retry and cancel of an ineligible job answer 409 instead of 400, with the same error body; cancel is also refused while the job uploads (`phase` is `upload`)
- A conversion job that exceeds its timeout ends `timed_out` and stays there until an operator retries it, instead of failing as retryable
- Remove the conversion `upload_pending` event kind; the end of conversion is recorded as `conversion_completed` while the job stays `running`, and a conversion job that times out records a `timed_out` event
- The baseline migration has a new revision id (`a62f1bf47735`); a database stamped at `fc430997788f` is refused and must be rebuilt
- The conversion worker refuses to start when `AIZK_WORKER_STALE_JOB_MINUTES` is at or below the job timeout plus the drain timeout and the cancel allowance; unset it to use the derived default (126 minutes at the default timeouts)
- Rename environment variables: `AIZK_GRAPH__CONTEXTUALIZATION__OPERATOR_API_HOST`, `_PORT`, and `_RELOAD` become `AIZK_SERVICE__OPERATOR_API_HOST`, `_PORT`, and `_RELOAD`; `AIZK_MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI`, `AIZK_MLFLOW_EXPERIMENT_NAME`, and `AIZK_MLFLOW_TRACING_ENABLED` become `AIZK_MLFLOW__TRACKING_URI`, `AIZK_MLFLOW__EXPERIMENT_NAME`, and `AIZK_MLFLOW__ENABLED`; the SQLite replication settings read the one `AIZK_S3_*` set; no old name is read
- Move each stage into its own package (`aizk.conversion`, `aizk.contextualization`, `aizk.extraction`), the shared stage kit into `aizk.pipeline`, process bootstrap into `aizk.service`, object storage into `aizk.storage`, and the operator app into `aizk.console`; the old import paths are removed without re-exports:
  - `aizk.conversion.auth` (now `aizk.service.auth`)
