- Logger names follow the new module paths; the old-to-new list is in the `stage-kit-and-layout` change's design document under `.specs/changes/archive/`, section "No public renames; logger names follow module paths"

### Added

- Chunking splitter foundation (`aizk.chunking`): document-structure splitter, chunk data model, deterministic identity
- Checkpoint validated contextualization model output (the document summary and each per-chunk revision) in a new `graph_contextualization_output_memo` table, so a retry of a partially-completed contextualization re-invokes the model only for outputs not already retained; consumed entries are pruned atomically with a successful persist
- Record a creation event with origin and principal on every graph work-unit creation (intake, the admission loop, backfill); the enqueue primitives return `(job, created)` so reuse of an existing unit writes no event
- Cap admission at a fixed batch per pass regardless of a stage's declared capacity, draining the remainder on later passes
- Record each stage's consumed content and produced-output fingerprint in run-input and applicability tables, so a downstream stage reconciles a byte-identical upstream regeneration against its active run without a model or extractor call
- Surface tri-state extraction currentness (current, needs reconciliation, stale) on the console, with re-extract eligible for the latter two states
- Conversion job responses carry `retry_class` (`retryable`, `permanent`, or null) and `phase` (`convert` or `upload` while `running`, else null); `GET /v1/jobs` filters by `retry_class`; status counts carry `failed_by_retry_class`
- Contextualization and extraction job responses carry `retry_class`, and their list routes filter by it
- Record a `requeued` event with the reason and the actor on every operator retry and re-admission, in every stage
- Cap automatic conversion attempts with `AIZK_WORKER_MAX_ATTEMPTS` (default 3)
- Count `pipeline.work_unit.finalize_skipped` (tags `stage`, `outcome`) when a unit's final write is skipped because another process already ended it, for example an operator cancel committed while the unit ran

### Changed

- Migrate the Docling figure converter off the deprecated `PictureItem.annotations` field to the `PictureItem.meta` API (`meta.classification`, `meta.description`)
- Derive derivation keys from the content a stage consumed and the configuration it ran under, rather than from upstream run keys, so an upstream regeneration that yields byte-identical input leaves the downstream key unchanged
- Derive the extraction pending backlog as a SQL anti-join over `pipeline_runs`, bounding the query at the requested limit instead of scanning the corpus in Python
- Keep the attempt count and `started_at` on operator retry and re-admission; the next claim increments the count
- Count `pipeline.work_unit.<outcome>` only when the unit's final write happened
- Stop a conversion upload at the job's deadline: past it, the job ends `timed_out` and its `timed_out` event records the `upload` phase
- A worker that is shut down with units still running ends them `failed` with `error_code` `worker_drain_terminated` and a retry wait that has already passed, so the next worker picks them up
- Stale-unit recovery writes the shared kit's `error_message` text; `error_code` is unchanged
- Delete a conversion job in any terminal status except `succeeded`, including `timed_out`
- The spawned conversion child logs in the configured structured format and stamps `job_id` on every record, so its INFO records, Docling's included, now reach the worker's output
- Move HTTP clients from `httpx` to `httpx2`; default TLS verification uses the operating system's trust store, and the User-Agent is `python-httpx2/<version>`; require `karakeep-client` 0.5.0

### Fixed

- Stop emitting a spurious `[Classification] <label>` line for every classified figure in converted Markdown; figure output is now the `<!-- Figure Type -->` / `<!-- Figure Description -->` comments only, matching the conversion-worker spec. Figure-bearing conversions now produce different output bytes, so their content hashes shift

---

## [0.1.3] - 2026-05-18

### Added

- Add append-only `conversion_job_events` audit table that records every conversion-job state transition, phase report, and source-enrichment outcome — run `alembic upgrade head` before starting the service
- Route every conversion-job status write (API submit, worker claim/recover/fail/succeed, UI bulk retry/cancel) through `record_transition`, co-committing one typed event row alongside each projection update
- Capture actor attribution on UI-initiated retry and cancel events by resolving the request `Principal` in the bulk-action route

---

## [0.1.2] - 2026-05-04

### Breaking Changes

- Replace the freeform `metadata.json` worker IPC payload with typed `SubprocessMetadata` (`extra="forbid"`); schema drift now raises a permanent `SubprocessMetadataInvalid` failure rather than re-queuing
- Change `ContentFetcher.fetch` and `RefResolver.resolve` signatures to thread `SourceMetadata` alongside `SourceRef`; replace `ConversionInput.metadata` (`dict[str, Any]`) with `source_meta: SourceMetadata` — out-of-tree adapters must adopt the new protocol

### Added

- Add `SourceMetadata` typed contract that flows through the resolver/fetcher chain with field-wise "earlier non-None wins" merge semantics, preserving resolver-supplied identity through later stages
- Extract `document_title` from converter output (first Docling `TitleItem`) and propagate it to the manifest, `ConversionOutput.title`, and the `Source` row
- Resolve relative links in converter output against the original `document_base_url` / `source_url` rather than the asset URL
- Surface enriched `Source.title` on the `/ui/jobs` view (preferred over `ConversionJob.title`) and include it in search-filter coverage

### Changed

- Make `KarakeepBookmarkResolver` the authoritative emitter of source identity (`source_url`, `document_base_url`, `normalized_url`, `resolver_title`) for every branch; fetchers only fill in URL fields the resolver did not supply
- Run `Source` row enrichment outside the manifest transaction so enrichment failures cannot block manifest writes or job output

### Fixed

- Truncate selected `source_title` to the `Source.title` column maximum (500 characters)
- Reject UUID-shaped and bare-URL strings as document titles; fall back to resolver-supplied title
- Guard `ArxivFetcher` URL backfill on resolver-supplied `source_url`, matching `UrlFetcher` and `GithubReadmeFetcher`
- Guard alembic against a missing `alembic_version` table during startup
- Update the conversion backfill notebook to use `source_ref` after the bookmark → source rename

---

## [0.1.1] - 2026-05-02

### Breaking Changes

- Rename environment variables to per-adapter nested namespaces — update existing `.env` files to the new naming convention before upgrading
- Replace bookmark-centric job submission and response fields with `source_ref` and manifest v2.0 payload format
- Rename `bookmarks` database table to `sources` — run `alembic upgrade head` before starting the service

### Added

- Add `Orchestrator` with injected fetch and convert dispatch, making adapter implementations swappable without modifying worker logic
- Add core ports package (protocols, types, registries, `SourceRef`) and discrete fetcher and converter adapter packages
- Add wiring package that assembles role-specific runtime configurations at startup
- Add `source_ref` (canonical identifier) and `source_ref_hash` (deduplication key) columns to the sources schema, both `NOT NULL`
- Add `converter_name` and `config_snapshot` fields to `ProcessResult` for result-to-configuration traceability
- Add hermetic test defaults: `env_file=None` and `app.state.config` injection before lifespan runs so local `.env` files do not affect test outcomes
- Add experimental Claimify pipeline for extracting atomic claims from source text (not yet wired into the main ingestion flow)

### Changed

- Base deduplication on canonical `SourceRef` values, improving idempotency across retries and re-submissions
- Expand pip-audit test coverage

### Fixed

- Fix fetch pipeline edge cases in HTTP error handling and `dotenv` loading
- Fix S3 artifact key storage — `markdown_key` and `manifest_key` now hold bare keys without path prefixes
- Fix suggestions job guard to use `BoundedSemaphore`, preventing over-subscription under concurrent load
- Fix import layering, HTML injection, and Source validation in the warnings subsystem

---

## [0.1.0] - 2026-04-14

### Added

- Add document conversion pipeline: fetch sources from KaraKeep, convert with Docling, store Markdown output and manifests in S3
- Add support for arXiv papers, URLs, and pre-crawled archive assets as conversion inputs
- Add GPU-aware subprocess scheduling for concurrent conversion jobs without GPU memory contention
- Add config snapshot recording per job — re-submitting the same source with the same configuration returns the cached result rather than reconverting
- Add REST API for job submission, status polling (atomic, no N+1 queries), retry, cancel, and aggregated status counts
- Add queue back-pressure to reject submissions when the worker is saturated
- Add HTMX jobs panel with sortable columns, bulk retry/cancel/delete, and date formatting
- Add stale job recovery at startup for jobs left in `running` state across restarts
- Add graceful shutdown on `SIGTERM`/`SIGINT` that drains in-flight jobs before exiting
- Add startup validation that checks external service availability before the worker begins polling
- Add explicit `retryable` attribute to all exception classes — non-retryable failures are not requeued
- Add subprocess traceback capture; failure detail is stored in the database for operator review
- Add Alembic migrations from a baseline schema with round-trip correctness tests
- Add Litestream continuous SQLite replication to S3 for point-in-time recovery
- Add liveness (`/health/live`) and readiness (`/health/ready`) health check endpoints
- Add MLflow tracing for upstream LLM and embedding calls with span-level detail
- Add non-root, multi-stage container image
- Add Podman Compose configuration for local and self-hosted deployment
- Add whitespace normalization for consistent Markdown output at document boundaries
- Add Granite 4.0-3B Vision model support with classification-based prompt routing
- Add ArXiv client with async support, automatic batching for metadata requests, enhanced ID validation, and context manager semantics
- Add review-first cleanup workflow for stale KaraKeep and AIZK entries

### Fixed

- Fix SQLite write safety with connection serialization
- Fix N+1 job listing query with eager loading
- Fix S3 hash deduplication and cancellation ordering edge cases in the worker

### Security

- Update dependencies to resolve known vulnerabilities detected by pip-audit

